ef 17592186520177 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520401 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520350 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520401 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520401 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520401 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186520092 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520401 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "70bd243f-e07d-55ba-afe6-e9424079d1a3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520423 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520046 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520423 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520423 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520118 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520423 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520146 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520423 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520270 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520423 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045493 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520423 #edb/ref 1077 "selection" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520423 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186520049 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520423 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "c6245f27-68e2-534e-b326-9a13a0b95dff" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520442 #edb/ref 1075 #edb/ref 17592186520113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520442 #edb/ref 1076 #edb/ref 17592186045492 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520442 #edb/ref 1077 "field-1" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520442 #edb/ref 1078 #edb/ref 17592186520113 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520442 #edb/ref 1079 #uuid "f7cb44d4-8640-5f83-ba9b-96604fc838db" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520475 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520376 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520475 #edb/ref 1069 "q-125986" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520475 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045486 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520475 #edb/ref 1071 "Using the definition of the hyperbolic cosine, calculate ${f}^{-1}(x)$ given that $f(x)=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+1)$ and $x\\ge -1.$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520475 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "7e900458-4a34-53b2-8b6d-fd38c3b57268" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520475 #edb/ref 1074 "Let $y=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(x+1).$ Since $x\\ge -1,$ we have $y\\ge 1.$\n\nTo find the inverse function we swap $x$ and $y:$ \n\n$$\nx=\\operatorname{cosh}⁡(y+1),\n$$\n\nwhere $x\\ge 1$ and $y\\ge -1.$\n\nNext, we apply the definition of $\\operatorname{cosh}⁡x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}x & =\\frac{1}{2}({e}^{y+1}+{e}^{-(y+1)}) \\\\ 2x & ={e}^{y+1}+{e}^{-(y+1)} \\\\ 2x{e}^{y+1} & ={e}^{2(y+1)}+1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nBringing everything to the left-hand side, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{e}^{2(y+1)}-2x{e}^{y+1}+1 & =0 \\\\ {({e}^{y+1})}^{2}-2x({e}^{y+1})+1 & =0.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nLet $Y={e}^{y+1}.$ We can form a quadratic equation in $Y$ and solve it by completing the square, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{Y}^{2}-2xY+1 & =0 \\\\ (Y-x)^{2}-{x}^{2}+1 & =0 \\\\ (Y-x)^{2} & ={x}^{2}-1 \\\\ Y-x & =\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1} \\\\ Y & =x\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1} \\\\ {e}^{y+1} & =x\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1} \\\\ y+1 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x\\pm \\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNote that for  $x\\ge 1,$ we have $x-\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\le 1$ and  $x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}\\ge 1.$ Since $y+1\\ge 0,$ the logarithm in the above equality must be non-negative. This requires its argument to be greater than or equal to $1$ for $x\\ge 1$, so we reject the alternative with the negative sign. This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}y+1 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}) \\\\ y & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1})-1\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n{f}^{-1}(x)=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1})-1.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520483 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520423 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520483 #edb/ref 1069 "q-125855" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520483 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520483 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\n$\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(-\\frac{15}{17})=$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520483 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "8ddac48b-cef1-5d70-9862-741511be4eb3" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520483 #edb/ref 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+x}{1-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(-\\frac{15}{17}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+(-\\frac{15}{17})}{1-(-\\frac{15}{17})}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1-\\frac{15}{17}}{1+\\frac{15}{17}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{2}{15}}{\\frac{32}{15}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1}{16}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡{2}^{-4} \\\\  & =-2\\operatorname{ln}⁡2.\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520485 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520370 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520485 #edb/ref 1069 "q-125859" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520485 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520485 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nGiven that $t>-\\frac{1}{2},$ which of the following is equivalent to $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{t}{t+1})?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520485 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9750db93-431a-52f4-a35e-36e894133bed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520485 #edb/ref 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{artanh}⁡x=\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+x}{1-x}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{artanh}⁡(\\frac{t}{t+1}) & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{1+\\frac{t}{t+1}}{1-\\frac{t}{t+1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{t+1+t}{t+1}}{\\frac{t+1-t}{t+1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\frac{\\frac{2t+1}{t+1}}{\\frac{1}{t+1}}) \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2t+1).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520502 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520442 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520502 #edb/ref 1069 "q-300604" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520502 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045485 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520502 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nEvaluate $\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡3.$ **Do not round** your answer.\n\n$\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡3=$\n{{field-1}}" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520502 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "da7e5a10-376b-5a22-a310-bd1bf7fa24cf" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520502 #edb/ref 1074 "By definition,\n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x=ln\\,(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡3 & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3+\\sqrt{{3}^{2}-1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3+\\sqrt{9-1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(3+\\sqrt{8}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520508 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186520401 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520508 #edb/ref 1069 "q-125854" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520508 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520508 #edb/ref 1071 "$$\n\nGiven that $y\\ge 1,$ which of the following is equivalent to $\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡\\sqrt{y}?$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520508 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "e77b2e22-83c2-5884-b6a1-4a4bd43f7297" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520508 #edb/ref 1074 "The definition of $\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x$ is \n\n$$\n\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡x=\\operatorname{ln}⁡(x+\\sqrt{{x}^{2}-1}).\n$$\n\nTherefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\operatorname{arcosh}⁡\\sqrt{y} & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{{(\\sqrt{y})}^{2}-1}) \\\\  & =\\operatorname{ln}⁡(\\sqrt{y}+\\sqrt{y-1}).\\end{aligned}\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520560 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186520574 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520560 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5ead7583-af5a-50aa-b7c8-b27d60003f5d" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520560 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186520475 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520573 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186520560 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186520573 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "75b8f4f6-638e-52c0-9e51-b84790620338" #edb/ref 